# Dual-Engine Quota Balancer (`dual-engine-quota-balancer`)

Running Gemini 4 Argon and Claude Fable simultaneously provides dual-model intelligence, but requires intelligent quota governance to prevent either provider from exhausting its rolling or daily window.

This skill balances task dispatch between Argon and Fable based on live telemetry metrics.

---

## 1. Provider Cost & Quota Economics

| Provider / Model | Quota Characteristics | Best Use Cases (Maximum ROI) | Throttle Threshold |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Gemini 4 Argon** (`pro`) | Rolling 5-Hour & Weekly limits; **95% prompt cache discount** ($0.10/MTok); 1M context. | Heavy asset parsing, broad file reading, Wine/Proton crash triage, image inspection. | Escalate/offload when 5h quota < 20% |
| **Claude Fable** (`claude`) | Daily & Weekly token allowances; high precision; strict output token cost. | Surgical C++ diffs, complex AST refactors, LuaJIT FFI bindings, compiler error fixes. | Escalate/offload when context > 80k or weekly < 25% |

---

## 2. Dynamic Workload Rebalancing Rules

1. **Shift QA & Log Reading to Argon:**
   - Always route compiler stdout logs, test suite output, and crash callstack analysis to Argon. Argon's 95% cache discount makes analyzing 100k lines of logs virtually free compared to Claude.
2. **Shift Surgical Diffs to Fable:**
   - Once Argon identifies the exact 10 lines causing a crash, route the surgical patch application to Fable. Fable’s atomic diff sequencer executes code fixes with near 100% first-turn accuracy.
3. **Emergency Offload:**
   - If Claude Fable approaches its daily quota ceiling:
     - Stage Fable's working state to `.agents/handoff.json`.
     - Route remaining tasks exclusively to Argon (`tandem-dispatch --to argon "<task>"`).
     - Argon completes the milestone while Claude's quota refreshes.
4. **Local CPU/iGPU/dGPU/RAM Offload & Repo Cheat Sheet (`dynamic-repo-model-cheatsheet`):**
   - Consult `agy-cheatsheet` (`cs`) for per-repository model and hardware routing (`Tandem•Arg+Fab` for `ogsr-complete-merge`, `Flash • Low` for config/UI repos).
   - Offload syntax validation (`local-ast-compiler`), semantic search (`local-rag`), `/dev/shm` builds (`ramdisk-tmpfs-build-bake-accelerator`), and dual-GPU workloads (`amd-igpu-nvidia-dgpu-hybrid-offload`) locally before spending either Gemini or Claude cloud quota.

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform CLI Interop (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- **Cross-OS Deployment (`install.ps1` & `install.sh`):** All CLI tools (`agy-cheatsheet` / `cs`, `repo-auto-sync`, `skill-evolve`, `skills-audit-update`, `adaptive-model-router`) run natively on Windows 10/11 via `.cmd`/PowerShell shims in `$HOME\.local\bin` and use `Path(tempfile.gettempdir())` instead of hardcoded `/tmp`.
- **Multi-Agent Split Terminal:** On Windows 10/11, use **Windows Terminal (`wt.exe`)** split panes (`wt -p "PowerShell" \; split-pane -V ...`) in place of Linux `tmux`/`kitty`, and `sccache` / MSVC `/MP` for shared build caching across git worktrees.
